For any types α and β, given a prior probability mass function `p : PMF α` and a channel/transition kernel `f : α → PMF β`:
if for every `b : β` in the support of the marginal distribution `p.bind f` (with witness `hb`), the posterior distribution `Cslib.Probability.PMF.posteriorDist p f b hb` is equal to the prior `p`,
then for all `a₀, a₁ : α` that belong to the support of `p`, the output distributions `f a₀` and `f a₁` are equal.

