declarations.reading:
Defines an inductive type family `DiamondPoset` parameterized by a natural number `j : ℕ`. For a given `j`, the type `DiamondPoset j` has three constructors:
- `bot`, taking no arguments;
- `mid`, taking an element of `Fin j`;
- `top`, taking no arguments.
The type automatically derives instances for `DecidableEq` and `Fintype`.

For each natural number `j`, defines a `PartialOrder` instance on `DiamondPoset j` where:
- `bot ≤ y` holds for all `y : DiamondPoset j`;
- `x ≤ top` holds for all `x : DiamondPoset j`;
- `mid a ≤ mid b` holds if and only if `a = b` (for `a, b : Fin j`);
- all other relations (e.g. `mid a ≤ bot`, `top ≤ mid b`, `top ≤ bot`) are false.

