`decay_ramsey_arrow a k` asserts that there exists a threshold natural number n₀ such that for every natural number n ≥ n₀, and for every coloring c : (completeGraph (Fin n)).edgeSet → ℕ+ of the edges of the complete graph on n vertices by positive integers:

if for every color i : ℕ+, the number of edges colored i is at most a(i) * (n.choose 2) (as real numbers),

then there exist a vertex subset s ⊆ Fin n of size k and a color i : ℕ+ such that every pair of distinct vertices u, v ∈ s is connected by an edge colored i (that is, s forms a monochromatic clique of size k in color i).

An inductive type `Handshake` parameterized by two types `V` and `Γ`, with two constructors:
- `single`, which takes an element `x : V`, a pair `a : Γ × Bool`, and an element `y : V`, returning `Handshake V Γ`;
- `double`, which takes an element `x : V`, two pairs `a : Γ × Bool` and `b : Γ × Bool`, and an element `y : V`, returning `Handshake V Γ`.

