1. For every natural number $i < m$, `cycle i` is the BRGC first rank of an $n$-bit necklace (that is: `cycle i < 2^n`, its binary reflected Gray code word is neither $0$ nor $2^n - 1$, and for every $s < cycle i$, the Gray code word of $s$ is not a cyclic rotation of the Gray code word of `cycle i`);
