Given a natural number `k`, `petersen_strip k` defines a simple graph on the vertex type `PetersenStripVertex` (consisting of vertices `u i` and `v i` for each integer `i`). 

Its adjacency relation is:
- `u i` and `u j` are adjacent if and only if `j = i + 1` or `j = i - 1`;
- `u i` and `v j` (and symmetrically `v i` and `u j`) are adjacent if and only if `j = i`;
- `v i` and `v j` are adjacent if and only if `k ≠ 0` and (`j = i + k` or `j = i - k`).

